<title>USA: Cyclone intensifying in Indian Ocean -WSC.</title>
<headline>Cyclone intensifying in Indian Ocean -WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Chantelle, with 75 mph winds, is strengthening in the South Indian Ocean near 9s/77e, private forecaster Weather Services Corporation (WSC) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The system will continue to intensify as it moves west southwest over open water, and top winds may be near 115 mph by 48 hours.</p>
